Force register operand for movq in THREAD_SETMEM to fix GCC 15 build.

glibc 2.12.1's nptl/sysdeps/x86_64/tls.h uses IMM_MODE ("nr" for PIC, "ir"
otherwise) as the operand constraint for both movl (32-bit) and movq (64-bit)
inline asm in THREAD_SETMEM and THREAD_SETMEM_NC. This permits the compiler
to bind the operand to either an immediate or a register.

GCC 15 (with default optimization) may bind a 64-bit value to a 32-bit-class
immediate or register operand, producing assembler output like:

    movq %eax,%fs:0x28

which the assembler rejects as "operand type mismatch for `movq'": you can
not use a 32-bit register with the 64-bit movq mnemonic. (Earlier GCC
versions happened to bind to %rax here, masking the issue.)

For the movq cases — where the value is an unsigned long int (64-bit on
x86_64) — restrict the constraint to "r" (register), so GCC always picks a
64-bit register. The movl cases keep IMM_MODE since 32-bit operand allows
either reg-or-imm freely.

This is a minimal, conservative fix. Upstream glibc later refactored the
THREAD_SETMEM family extensively (3.x), but for the 2.12 backport we only
touch the two movq lines.

--- a/nptl/sysdeps/x86_64/tls.h	2010-05-04 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/nptl/sysdeps/x86_64/tls.h	2026-05-09 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
@@ -278,7 +278,7 @@
 	   abort ();							      \
 									      \
 	 asm volatile ("movq %q0,%%fs:%P1" :				      \
-		       : IMM_MODE ((unsigned long int) value),		      \
+		       : "r" ((unsigned long int) value),		      \
 			 "i" (offsetof (struct pthread, member)));	      \
        }})

@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@
 	   abort ();							      \
 									      \
 	 asm volatile ("movq %q0,%%fs:%P1(,%q2,8)" :			      \
-		       : IMM_MODE ((unsigned long int) value),		      \
+		       : "r" ((unsigned long int) value),		      \
 			 "i" (offsetof (struct pthread, member[0])),	      \
 			 "r" (idx));					      \
        }})
